&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_actions__container c-message__actions&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Account Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team: Partnerships / Channel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: [NYC] - Hybrid&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: Head of Partnerships or VP, Channels&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Lightning AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lightning AI is building the platform and infrastructure that make it dramatically easier for teams to develop, train, deploy, and scale AI systems. As the company behind PyTorch Lightning, and following our merger with Voltage Park, we bring together developer-first AI tooling with high-performance compute infrastructure for researchers, startups, and enterprises building at the frontier of AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate with a simple set of values: Move Fast, Focus, Balance, Craftsmanship, and Minimal. We care about people who can operate with urgency, solve hard problems directly, and build with high standards without creating unnecessary complexity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Partner Account Manager to help build Lightning AI’s partner ecosystem and turn strategic partnerships into real revenue. This role will own relationships with channel, cloud, reseller, services, and technology partners, and will be responsible for building joint pipeline, aligning field teams, and making partners successful in positioning Lightning AI to customers building serious AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Own a portfolio of strategic partners and build clear joint business plans tied to pipeline, revenue, customer adoption, and field engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Create and execute co-selling motions with partner sales teams, Lightning AI Account Executives, Solutions Engineering, Marketing, and Customer Success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Identify partner-sourced and partner-influenced opportunities, qualify fit, and help move deals through the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Develop partner account plans, executive alignment maps, target account lists, enablement plans, and quarterly business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Work with Channel MLSEs and Partner Enablement to ensure partner teams understand Lightning AI’s technical value proposition and how to identify strong-fit customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Negotiate and operationalize partner motions, including referral, resale, co-sell, marketplace, implementation, and services workflows where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Track partner performance, pipeline health, sourced revenue, influenced revenue, activation, and engagement quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Represent partner feedback internally and help improve partner programs, packaging, integrations, and field processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; 5+ years in partnerships, channel sales, business development, alliances, enterprise sales, or partner account management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Experience building revenue-producing partnerships in technical B2B markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; Strong commercial instincts and the ability to turn partner relationships into pipeline, opportunities, and closed revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
